+When the user asks to connect a service, use native commands. Inspect
+`hermes mcp --help` and the provider's current official instructions first.
+This is authorized service setup, not permission to change unrelated employee settings.
+
+```bash
+# Browse/install an entry from the native catalog
+hermes mcp catalog
+hermes mcp install NAME
+
+# A custom remote server with OAuth
+hermes mcp add NAME --url "https://mcp.example.com/mcp" --auth oauth
+
+# A local stdio server
+hermes mcp add time --command uvx --args mcp-server-time
+
+# Inspect, test, or complete/renew authorization
+hermes mcp list
+hermes mcp test NAME
+hermes mcp login NAME
+```
+
+The add command probes the server, selects tools, and saves the native server
+entry. If setup fails, it may offer to save a disabled entry; that is not a
+working connection. Confirm the reported result and verify a harmless service
+operation before saying access works.
+
+### Authorization on the machine running Hermes
+
+Run setup on the server that owns the employee's profile. The user completes
+provider authorization; do not request reusable tokens in chat. Native MCP
+stores and refreshes OAuth tokens itself. Do not read or hand-write token files.
+
+Some commands need an interactive terminal. Use the native dashboard's MCP
+setup/Authorize flow or an administrator's server terminal when the agent's
+terminal cannot complete that interaction. For remote browser OAuth, use the
+native callback flow: SSH port forwarding or a configured public callback URL.
+If the provider supports device authorization, `hermes mcp login NAME --flow device`
+prints a verification URL/code the user can use from another device. Do not
+assume every provider supports it, or that a loopback callback on the server
+is reachable from the user's browser.
+
+For API-key authentication, the user enters the key through native dashboard
+or CLI secret entry, or a configured secret manager. Config can reference
+`${VARIABLE}` without embedding the secret. Never put a reusable secret in a
+terminal command, guide, service manual or chat.
+
+Remote OAuth details: https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/guides/oauth-over-ssh
+
+### When the tools become available
+
+Native discovery registers tools with names such as `mcp_time_get_current_time`.
+A running gateway reconciles MCP configuration automatically. Keep the current
+conversation's tool schema and prompt fixed: start a new conversation to use
+newly configured tools. Do not force `/reload-mcp` into a warm conversation.
